Third-party references and attribution
======================================

This repository contains original example code written for study purposes.
Some examples follow ideas, tutorials or model architectures published by
others. No upstream source code, dataset or pretrained weight is
redistributed here; the implementations were written or reworked for this
repository.

PixelCNN
--------
`examples/mnist_generative/pixelcnn_mnist.py` follows the masked-convolution
idea introduced by van den Oord et al., "Conditional Image Generation with
PixelCNN Decoders" (arXiv:1606.05328), and the public PyTorch implementation
jzbontar/pixelcnn-pytorch (MIT License) was used as a design reference.
The implementation here was rewritten; see the upstream repository for its
license:
https://github.com/jzbontar/pixelcnn-pytorch

Diffusion model
---------------
`examples/mnist_generative/mnist_diffusion.py` follows the DDPM formulation
(Ho et al., "Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models", arXiv:2006.11239).
The U-Net is written in this repository for demonstration purposes.

VQ-VAE
------
`examples/mnist_generative/vqvae_mnist.py` follows van den Oord et al.,
"Neural Discrete Representation Learning" (arXiv:1711.00937). The
implementation was rewritten from the paper and from public educational
material (including d2l.ai).

DeepONet / PINN / PINO
----------------------
The scientific-ML examples follow:
  - Lu et al., "DeepONet: Learning nonlinear operators ..." (arXiv:1910.03193)
  - Raissi et al., "Physics-informed neural networks" (arXiv:1711.10561)
  - Li et al., "Physics-Informed Neural Operator for Learning Partial
    Differential Equations" (arXiv:2111.03794)

The vendored DeepXDE source tree that accompanied the original study
workspace is not redistributed. DeepXDE is licensed under the LGPL-2.1; see
https://github.com/lululxvi/deepxde for the original project.

